.TH PERF_EVENT_OPEN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
perf_event_open \- Linux x86-64 syscall 298
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int perf_event_open(const void* attributes, pid_t process, int cpu, int group, unsigned long flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a performance event. The caller must provide a kernel-compatible perf_event_attr including its size; policy often restricts access.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR perf_event_open (2)
